WEBVTT

00:00.470 --> 00:03.730
A few days ago

00:05.440 --> 00:08.980
I am here! Like I am every day!

00:08.980 --> 00:11.690
Detective Tsukauchi...
and the principal, too?

00:12.110 --> 00:14.360
Are you here about Aoyama?

00:16.100 --> 00:18.060
And what comes after.

00:18.060 --> 00:21.860
Right now, we are only telling
a select number of people.

02:00.940 --> 02:02.900
First, there is the fact that currently,

02:03.240 --> 02:07.860
the pro heroes are searching
high and low for All For One,

02:07.860 --> 02:10.990
but their chances of finding
him seem very low.

02:11.750 --> 02:14.320
Bakugo said something like that, too...

02:14.320 --> 02:17.100
But to hear it all laid out like that...

02:17.100 --> 02:18.690
Does it mean there's no point?

02:18.950 --> 02:22.320
No, it's the opposite. It'll tie
together with Eraser's plan.

02:22.700 --> 02:25.650
As Class A's homeroom
teacher, I have an idea.

02:26.250 --> 02:28.460
With Mr. Aizawa's plan...

02:28.750 --> 02:32.170
In order to draw out a cunning coward,

02:32.170 --> 02:35.410
you have to slowly soften his heart.

02:35.720 --> 02:38.840
So pretend like "We've searched
desperately but still can't find him.

02:38.840 --> 02:40.940
What the hell, scum?"

02:40.940 --> 02:42.580
That's an interesting way to put it.

02:43.150 --> 02:46.050
We'll proceed on the assumption
that Search is working.

02:46.050 --> 02:50.680
All For One should be minutely
aware of all our movements.

02:51.190 --> 02:53.970
We'll show him that our efforts
since Midoriya's return

02:53.970 --> 02:56.180
are resulting in frustration
and exhaustion.

02:56.640 --> 02:59.500
We'll make him think we're making
one bad move after another

02:59.500 --> 03:02.400
and make him feel good thinking everything
is going according to his plan.

03:02.750 --> 03:06.830
We'll use Eraser's plan to
use the informant, Aoyama,

03:06.830 --> 03:09.790
to lure All For One somewhere.

03:09.790 --> 03:11.930
We're trying to increase that
plan's chances of success.

03:12.790 --> 03:14.420
Then, Aoyama is--

03:19.480 --> 03:21.350
I'm so glad!

03:22.840 --> 03:25.250
Aoyama...!

03:25.250 --> 03:29.270
Excuse me, but what about
what Aoyama's father said?

03:29.880 --> 03:31.920
If we failed, we would be killed.

03:31.920 --> 03:34.270
If we lied, we would be killed.

03:34.840 --> 03:36.910
That's what he said.

03:36.910 --> 03:40.060
If we don't know how he
can tell what is a lie,

03:40.060 --> 03:43.740
then isn't there still some danger
to Aoyama and his family?

03:44.080 --> 03:45.730
We have a plan for that, too.

03:46.350 --> 03:48.220
According to Mr. and Mrs. Aoyama,

03:48.220 --> 03:51.630
All For One only contacts
them through a voice call.

03:51.630 --> 03:53.400
They have no written contact.

03:53.890 --> 03:55.760
He likely has many other such "friends,"

03:55.760 --> 03:59.590
so I don't think he scrutinizes everything
they say carefully before acting.

04:00.070 --> 04:04.380
His system can probably tell immediately
by their voices if someone is lying.

04:04.650 --> 04:08.130
Therefore, if there is
no lie in that audio,

04:08.130 --> 04:10.400
then he can show up without fear.

04:10.400 --> 04:12.780
That's why we'll use Aizawa's idea,

04:12.780 --> 04:14.300
and use HIM!

04:15.520 --> 04:16.730
C'mon!

04:20.780 --> 04:21.700
Hey.

04:21.700 --> 04:23.530
Shinso!

04:23.930 --> 04:25.820
Your costume's so cool!

04:26.260 --> 04:30.560
I was surprised when I heard the
details of the plan from Mr. Aizawa.

04:30.560 --> 04:32.820
Because during the combat battles...

04:33.450 --> 04:37.190
However, I cannot make the
person I brainwash talk.

04:37.190 --> 04:40.920
Also, orders that require
them to think won't work.

04:41.280 --> 04:43.630
I thought that was what you said.

04:44.220 --> 04:45.780
Look at this mess.

04:46.410 --> 04:49.160
I thought I'd be transferring
to the hero course in April

04:49.160 --> 04:51.470
and competing with you all.

04:52.000 --> 04:55.640
I kept training to improve my
Quirk so I could do that,

04:55.640 --> 04:58.430
but I didn't think we wouldn't be
able to move on to the next grade.

04:58.430 --> 05:02.220
Improve your Quirk? So you really can...?

05:02.700 --> 05:04.820
Yeah, I can do it.

05:05.410 --> 05:08.410
If I control Aoyama and his
parents and make them talk,

05:09.120 --> 05:12.990
then neither my will nor their
feelings will get in the way.

05:12.990 --> 05:15.470
Wow!

05:15.470 --> 05:18.990
But in order to do that,
it's harder to activate.

05:18.990 --> 05:20.140
You're amazing!

05:20.140 --> 05:22.010
Thanks, Shinso!

05:22.010 --> 05:24.430
Will you be in Class A? Class B?

05:24.430 --> 05:25.460
Join Class A! A!

05:25.460 --> 05:26.600
What's your hero name?

05:26.980 --> 05:28.330
They're so cheerful...

05:28.330 --> 05:30.100
What's with these guys?

05:30.370 --> 05:35.390
Shinso was able to train his
Quirk thanks to Aizawa's help.

05:35.700 --> 05:38.300
Mr. Aizawa really is amazing!

05:38.710 --> 05:42.440
By the way, Shinso doesn't have
his provisional license yet,

05:42.440 --> 05:44.090
but since it's an emergency,

05:44.090 --> 05:47.810
we got special permission from
the acting chairman, Mera.

05:47.810 --> 05:49.060
Whoa!

05:49.530 --> 05:52.530
But isn't the problem what comes next?

05:52.530 --> 05:55.690
We're supposed to lure out the villains
and round them all up at once?

05:55.690 --> 05:56.630
Is that possible?

05:57.090 --> 05:58.380
Even if there are less heroes now,

05:58.730 --> 06:01.380
if a large number of us
gather in one place,

06:01.380 --> 06:03.050
then won't that give us away?

06:03.600 --> 06:06.520
It'll be fine if they aren't there.

06:06.520 --> 06:10.390
In order to make that work, there's
another key person we need.

06:14.920 --> 06:17.280
This is a request from All
Might and the others.

06:17.670 --> 06:19.890
This is a crucial job.

06:21.000 --> 06:22.090
Can you do it...

06:22.590 --> 06:23.930
Phantom Thief?

06:27.320 --> 06:32.260
"You have a few days to Copy this
person's Quirk and learn to use it."

06:32.690 --> 06:34.160
Are you kidding?

06:34.870 --> 06:36.290
Sorry.

06:37.060 --> 06:39.350
My voice didn't reach him.

06:40.060 --> 06:42.710
Tell me! Who altered you?!

06:43.660 --> 06:48.450
I am Kurogiri, the protector
of Tomura Shigaraki.

06:48.960 --> 06:52.420
You were in Class 2-A at U.A. High School!

06:52.420 --> 06:54.930
We were all going to become heroes!

06:54.930 --> 06:57.000
You're Oboro Shirakumo!

06:58.460 --> 07:03.610
Besides, we still don't know if this
guy is Kurogiri or Shirakumo.

07:04.220 --> 07:08.330
I've lost one eye, and my
Erasure is barely working.

07:08.850 --> 07:10.440
In the next battle,

07:10.440 --> 07:12.380
I won't be able to do anything.

07:17.530 --> 07:18.700
I heard that at Jaku,

07:19.510 --> 07:22.920
without Eraser Head, we
would've been wiped out.

07:25.040 --> 07:27.120
I was always told as a kid

07:27.840 --> 07:31.130
that I couldn't be a
superhero with my Quirk.

07:32.320 --> 07:35.260
That it was a Quirk for a side character...

07:43.170 --> 07:44.330
Monoma.

07:45.340 --> 07:48.440
This plan won't work if
we're missing anyone.

07:48.790 --> 07:51.640
I can bring him out. Just tell me when.

07:58.760 --> 08:00.600
There are no side characters here.

08:02.990 --> 08:04.500
Up until now...

08:04.500 --> 08:05.840
And from now on...

08:07.240 --> 08:08.660
You're the star!

08:13.370 --> 08:16.170
I'm pulling the strings!

08:16.470 --> 08:20.470
Division

08:21.150 --> 08:24.510
As expected, he brought
a large army with him.

08:24.870 --> 08:26.260
All squads, move!

08:26.550 --> 08:30.620
If he gets One For All, then there's no
need for him to run and hide anymore!

08:32.120 --> 08:33.490
We'll end it here...

08:35.100 --> 08:37.480
and this is where we're planning to start!

08:49.040 --> 08:49.710
Dabi.

08:49.710 --> 08:52.100
Don't tell me what to do, Leader!

08:52.370 --> 08:54.760
I didn't think I'd get to see you here,

08:54.760 --> 08:56.630
Dad!

08:56.630 --> 08:59.370
But first, a funeral for your friends?

09:09.330 --> 09:11.190
I won't let you,

09:11.590 --> 09:13.190
idiot brother!

09:13.190 --> 09:15.360
Shoto!

09:16.440 --> 09:18.590
You're gathering in droves...

09:19.270 --> 09:22.820
Are you planning a free-for-all here?

09:23.250 --> 09:24.950
Activate Operation Troy!

09:33.250 --> 09:34.290
Cages?

09:35.880 --> 09:37.970
You think these'll hold us?

09:38.660 --> 09:43.240
They should know that these will
be torn apart in a second.

09:43.770 --> 09:46.740
So why did they use it
at such a large scale?

09:46.740 --> 09:49.860
It'll work this time, All Might.

09:50.980 --> 09:54.630
It's a plan we all refined together.

09:54.630 --> 09:56.360
I'm sure it'll go well.

09:57.090 --> 09:59.580
We weren't able to bring him down before.

09:59.960 --> 10:01.850
Your stomach was gouged out.

10:02.600 --> 10:05.230
But you and I are both still alive!

10:05.230 --> 10:07.730
We can do it this time, All Might!

10:08.230 --> 10:09.130
Yeah.

10:09.790 --> 10:12.040
I see, All Might.

10:12.660 --> 10:14.390
I know what you're after.

10:14.700 --> 10:18.200
Away from U.A., away from
the makeshift fortress.

10:18.200 --> 10:20.100
We needed to do all this!

10:21.180 --> 10:22.420
To make you overconfident

10:22.810 --> 10:24.510
and draw you out.

10:24.510 --> 10:25.950
And then--

10:25.950 --> 10:27.610
I'm pulling the strings!

10:33.400 --> 10:34.780
Now, everyone!

10:35.860 --> 10:38.320
Get in there!

10:38.800 --> 10:43.640
You're trying to split us up!

10:49.670 --> 10:52.040
Neito Monoma

10:55.510 --> 10:57.520
The cage is moving?

10:57.520 --> 11:00.190
You think these things will hold us?!

11:00.600 --> 11:01.700
Break them.

11:04.390 --> 11:05.670
Hurry.

11:08.880 --> 11:10.430
Cages like this...

11:10.430 --> 11:12.700
...won't last three seconds!

11:14.730 --> 11:16.400
Those three seconds...

11:16.710 --> 11:18.470
...were what we wanted!

11:18.970 --> 11:20.900
We just need three seconds.

11:22.290 --> 11:24.310
Limit their movements...

11:26.150 --> 11:27.880
and split them up.

11:31.020 --> 11:32.910
We'll get the first move by seconds!

11:33.620 --> 11:34.450
Deku!

11:34.450 --> 11:35.230
Right!

11:36.460 --> 11:40.840
It's all to make you go through
the warp gates at the same time

11:40.840 --> 11:43.380
and make sure to split you up!

11:45.780 --> 11:47.880
I'm pulling the strings!

11:48.250 --> 11:49.620
This is stupid!

11:49.620 --> 11:53.230
How much money did you waste just
to do this, you money worshippers?!

11:53.230 --> 11:58.030
Well, we have a countermeasure
against Shigaraki's Decay, too!

11:58.030 --> 12:00.560
You just keep brazenly showing up,

12:00.560 --> 12:03.000
but we'll send you scattering!

12:17.540 --> 12:19.920
What... the...?

12:20.740 --> 12:22.140
We can do this!

12:22.490 --> 12:25.040
Get 'em!

12:26.240 --> 12:27.270
Huh?

12:29.170 --> 12:30.020
De--

12:38.660 --> 12:39.640
Fat!

12:39.640 --> 12:42.270
Get the ones who're left! Take command!

12:42.270 --> 12:44.190
I'm leaving Young Aoyama to you!

12:44.660 --> 12:45.540
Roger!

12:48.270 --> 12:50.040
"We will defeat you here!"

12:50.040 --> 12:51.730
That was a good bluff!

12:51.730 --> 12:54.120
M-M-M-Merci!

12:54.120 --> 12:56.830
Young Monoma, return to Aizawa!

12:56.830 --> 12:57.750
Yup.

12:59.140 --> 13:00.810
We've successfully split them up!

13:01.270 --> 13:05.140
We will now move on to Phase 2!

13:09.350 --> 13:12.850
Gunga Villa Site

13:16.850 --> 13:18.370
This is...

13:19.060 --> 13:20.360
Welcome!

13:25.670 --> 13:27.620
Gunga Villa...

13:28.690 --> 13:30.070
I see.

13:30.360 --> 13:32.160
Sorry, Endeavor.

13:32.160 --> 13:36.380
I guess he's not going to come wearing
stuff that I can cut through.

13:36.380 --> 13:38.620
Don't worry. I wasn't expecting you to.

13:39.880 --> 13:42.080
We figured out that the sludgy Warp you have

13:42.080 --> 13:44.170
is a lesser version of Kurogiri's

13:44.170 --> 13:46.380
at the battle in Camino.

13:47.020 --> 13:49.540
The warping distance is much shorter,

13:49.540 --> 13:51.480
and you can't warp yourself.

13:51.940 --> 13:55.420
The U.A. Barrier was also strengthened
to account for that.

13:55.420 --> 13:58.930
This is all a result of your conceit,
the consequences of your own actions!

13:59.730 --> 14:03.180
Splitting us up and
attacking us separately.

14:03.180 --> 14:05.160
It's a great plan!

14:05.160 --> 14:09.680
But you need to take into consideration
whether or not you can win.

14:10.500 --> 14:16.370
Even if you split up your forces
because you've lost so many heroes,

14:16.370 --> 14:19.990
you really are a cruel man, Endeavor.

14:20.430 --> 14:23.580
Did you pit One For All against Tomura?

14:23.580 --> 14:25.590
That's a huge risk.

14:26.220 --> 14:27.710
Moreover,

14:26.300 --> 14:31.510
Camino Ward

14:28.130 --> 14:31.920
there's the cruelest matchup of all--

14:32.400 --> 14:36.550
Putting your youngest child in the difficult
situation of cleaning up your mess,

14:36.550 --> 14:40.130
and continuing the abuse
against your eldest!

14:40.990 --> 14:43.190
We've split up the villains
according to plan!

14:43.710 --> 14:46.770
It appears the fighting has
commenced at each location.

14:47.100 --> 14:50.160
The real battle starts now, All Might.

14:50.160 --> 14:50.910
Yeah.

14:55.910 --> 14:59.710
Sky above U.A. High

15:11.560 --> 15:13.130
U.A.?

15:13.130 --> 15:14.640
What is this place?

15:19.540 --> 15:21.040
Denim Head, this is bad!

15:21.750 --> 15:22.820
They got us!

15:23.140 --> 15:24.090
Deku's--

15:26.650 --> 15:29.650
Okuto Island

15:35.470 --> 15:37.150
Deku's not here!

15:37.580 --> 15:38.650
Deku?!

15:39.040 --> 15:40.180
Why?

15:40.180 --> 15:42.190
Shouldn't you be with Shigaraki?

15:42.960 --> 15:46.450
Danger Sense didn't activate...!

15:50.760 --> 15:53.520
Himiko Toga...

15:54.440 --> 15:56.220
Deku's not here?

15:56.600 --> 15:57.650
What happened?

15:57.650 --> 15:58.850
I don't know!

15:58.850 --> 16:00.570
He was pulled somewhere else!

16:00.570 --> 16:02.620
I-I-Isn't this bad?

16:02.620 --> 16:04.900
Without him, we can't fight
like we were planning.

16:04.900 --> 16:06.240
We have to tell the others!

16:06.840 --> 16:09.000
Whatever, let's just do this!

16:09.000 --> 16:10.560
It's already started--

16:10.970 --> 16:15.760
The fight against the greatest
villain in recorded history!

16:18.060 --> 16:20.540
The ground's so far down...

16:21.060 --> 16:22.600
I'm in the sky.

16:22.600 --> 16:23.840
Floating.

16:25.920 --> 16:29.700
No Jailbreakers or Front
members were brought here.

16:30.260 --> 16:31.430
Just me.

16:32.130 --> 16:33.580
Oh well.

16:34.310 --> 16:38.140
Don't get in my way this time, Me.

16:55.600 --> 16:57.180
An electromagnetic barrier!

16:57.840 --> 16:59.770
My body's getting stiff.

17:00.490 --> 17:01.270
But--

17:01.570 --> 17:02.530
Whoa, there!

17:04.310 --> 17:05.320
You're fraying apart!

17:08.130 --> 17:10.630
As long as you're moving with
your brain and muscles,

17:10.630 --> 17:14.140
a strong electrical current running
through your body will stiffen you up.

17:14.140 --> 17:16.110
No matter how strong you are,

17:16.110 --> 17:17.640
it'll work for at least a second!

17:18.890 --> 17:23.940
Blocks from the ground fly up
and disintegrate in the sky...

17:25.270 --> 17:28.390
They installed this to prevent
Decay from spreading, huh?

17:29.110 --> 17:29.930
But--

17:30.440 --> 17:32.360
That will lead to your ruin.

17:32.360 --> 17:33.900
Jeanist.

17:34.550 --> 17:36.240
We're floating in the sky, right?

17:36.630 --> 17:38.610
If you use up your ground that fast,

17:38.610 --> 17:41.260
your precious stage will disappear!

17:41.870 --> 17:43.610
No need to worry.

17:44.550 --> 17:46.720
We have plenty of raw material.

17:47.520 --> 17:49.890
Don't you understand yet, Shigaraki?

17:49.890 --> 17:51.580
Has your brain short-circuited?

17:52.090 --> 17:58.300
Coffin in the Sky

17:52.400 --> 17:55.470
This place was created to defeat you--

17:55.470 --> 17:57.130
the Coffin in the Sky!

18:03.810 --> 18:07.850
Plates F10-35 and G10-45 have been damaged.

18:08.180 --> 18:10.560
Okay, we'll replace them right away!

18:10.930 --> 18:12.100
Let's go, everyone!

18:12.100 --> 18:12.920
Okay!

18:13.570 --> 18:15.180
Parts please.

18:16.520 --> 18:19.450
Um, what was your name again?

18:19.970 --> 18:21.200
Creaty.

18:21.530 --> 18:23.630
My friends call me Yao-momo!

18:23.630 --> 18:25.400
Please call me what you wish.

18:26.210 --> 18:28.780
With your widespread attacks
that cause instant death

18:28.780 --> 18:31.210
and speed of All Might at his peak,

18:32.050 --> 18:35.050
we needed to figure out
where to detain you.

18:36.190 --> 18:40.770
The two battles we fought against you
after you awakened showed us the way.

18:42.150 --> 18:43.440
That's pretty good.

18:43.810 --> 18:45.880
Let's make it fly!

18:46.370 --> 18:49.470
A mere 16-year-old girl made this possible.

18:50.460 --> 18:53.060
The evacuation system
suggested by the principal

18:53.060 --> 18:54.810
was added to the countermeasures
against Decay.

18:55.670 --> 18:58.050
Splitting the area blocks
into even smaller sections

18:58.050 --> 19:00.350
and turning them into drones
with an upgraded program.

19:01.260 --> 19:04.280
There weren't enough raw materials due
to the collapse of the supply chain,

19:06.660 --> 19:08.650
it needed to be constructed
in a short timeframe,

19:10.720 --> 19:15.760
and a lot of energy was needed for its
movement and the electromagnetic barrier.

19:16.910 --> 19:19.850
Wow! Manga, isn't this crazy?

19:19.850 --> 19:21.250
You feeling it?

19:21.250 --> 19:22.900
It's like I'm screaming "Whoa!"

19:22.550 --> 19:27.140
Whoa

19:22.900 --> 19:24.270
First years! Focus!

19:24.270 --> 19:27.140
We're basically second years,
though. Right, Manga?

19:27.140 --> 19:28.810
We're the cornerstones!

19:28.810 --> 19:31.530
Let's do our best so we can
keep Shigaraki locked up!

19:31.530 --> 19:33.450
Yeah!

19:33.450 --> 19:37.030
Charge your best, Chargebolt!

19:37.560 --> 19:40.300
Everything that we've done up until now

19:40.300 --> 19:42.490
is powering this coffin!

19:43.580 --> 19:45.700
It's not for fame or glory.

19:46.300 --> 19:49.790
We are just doing this because
we want to protect the future.

19:50.520 --> 19:52.180
We are the ones

19:52.860 --> 19:54.720
who will stop your destruction!

20:13.130 --> 20:15.570
It's time to stop showing off your toys.

20:15.570 --> 20:16.940
With a shock wave...

20:16.940 --> 20:18.240
It's no use!

20:18.240 --> 20:21.100
Did you forget the shitty
game we played at Jaku?

20:23.760 --> 20:25.020
My Quirk...

20:33.850 --> 20:38.570
You don't like Erasure,
right, Mr. Last Boss?

20:38.570 --> 20:40.330
Don't move. You'll be out of position.

20:41.770 --> 20:46.820
I can't move, but as long as I
keep contact with him like this,

20:46.820 --> 20:50.400
Monoma can use Copy past his
limit of five minutes.

20:51.120 --> 20:54.740
We were supposed to create an advantageous
situation for Midoriya like this

20:54.740 --> 20:56.970
with him at the center of the operation.

20:57.410 --> 20:58.760
But...

20:59.160 --> 21:01.910
This is bad. Midoriya's not here.

21:02.290 --> 21:03.830
On top of that,

21:04.400 --> 21:09.080
back then, Shigaraki's
body wasn't complete.

21:23.800 --> 21:26.380
Dynamight, what's that?
What can you tell us?

21:26.380 --> 21:27.930
Dunno! Never seen it--

21:37.410 --> 21:40.800
I thought you were cool...

21:41.760 --> 21:45.320
I'm really disappointed,

21:46.950 --> 21:49.160
Eraser Head.

23:20.000 --> 23:22.000
Preview

23:21.070 --> 23:21.990
Here's the preview!

23:22.750 --> 23:25.590
The intense decisive battle continues.

23:26.100 --> 23:30.560
Even though the heroes' plan to
separate the villains succeeded,

23:30.920 --> 23:33.680
I was the only one who didn't end
up where I was supposed to be.

23:34.690 --> 23:36.520
Get back, Izuku Midoriya!

23:36.880 --> 23:38.760
To protect everyone!

23:39.580 --> 23:41.680
Next time, "Inflation."

23:42.260 --> 23:45.990
That girl sings of love
in the midst of war.

23:45.980 --> 23:49.980
Next time: Inflation

23:46.610 --> 23:48.230
Go beyond!

23:48.230 --> 23:49.610
Plus Ultra!
